From: A50 Ubuntu Touch development
Subject: [PATCH] Backport Halium 13 recording AudioFlinger lookup removal

Halium 13's recording patch already initializes af to nullptr in
AudioSystem::getInputFramesLost. Apply the same correction after the
Halium 11 hybris recording patch, where the call is left active despite
its result being unused. No AudioFlinger service runs in this recording
path, so the lookup stalls the callback while holding the AudioSource
lock and prevents video Stop from completing.

Upstream: Halium/hybris-patches, halium-13.0, frameworks/av/0004-halium-get-rid-of-using-AudioFlinger-for-recording.patch
Base: GSI 1542 frameworks/av 18186d8f9b4dcaff242ae9ea9b74e6827f14a1cc
Apply after the standard Halium 11 hybris patches.

--- a/media/libaudioclient/AudioSystem.cpp
+++ b/media/libaudioclient/AudioSystem.cpp
@@ -508,7 +508,7 @@
 
 uint32_t AudioSystem::getInputFramesLost(audio_io_handle_t ioHandle)
 {
-    const sp<IAudioFlinger>& af = AudioSystem::get_audio_flinger();
+    const sp<IAudioFlinger>& af = nullptr; /*AudioSystem::get_audio_flinger();*/
     uint32_t result = 0;
     /*if (af == 0) return result;
     if (ioHandle == AUDIO_IO_HANDLE_NONE) return result;
